Cuboidz wrote:
> 1) How thoroughly do you search each dungeon level before continuing
> to the next?

Depends on the situation.  If it's very early and food is an issue,
I'll keep moving as long as I've located the stairs.  Once I have a
food ration, I'll definitely try to find any shops, and I'll explore
fairly thoroughly, until I've got a pretty reasonable set of
equipment.  After that, I'll just head for the Castle (or whatever the
next goal is) without mapping out every level.  I'll rarely bother
searching most of Gehennom--just go ahead and ascend at that point.

So basically, explore reasonably thoroughly early on (don't go
searching everywhere, but if there's something obvious then go
ahead).  Later on, when you're well outfitted and ready to ascend
without more resources, just go down.

> Do you try to discover all secret rooms (including shops
> and vaults)?

Vaults, not so much unless I happen to have magic mapping or have a
real need for money (e.g. haven't gotten the 1st buy of protection
yet).

Shops are always worth finding, especially early on.  But if you're in
an early food crunch you may go ahead and come back in the near
future.

> Also, how many times do you search one spot before
> deciding nothing's there (using "n[number]s")?

I usually use "9s", but I'll do it  again if I'm pretty sure from the
layout that there's something there (I use the default key setup,
"n9s" would have me walking southeast before searching 9 times!)

> 2) Is "leveling" a good idea in nethack, e.g. running around until you
> see a monster to kill (to gain experience)?
>

That's usually a bad idea.  It might make sense in limited
circumstances (e.g. if you're going to gain an intrinsic next level,
and there's some monster near the start of the next level that
intrinsic will help against).  Normally you want to level somewhat
naturally, keep amassing more equipment to go along with your levels.

I find even the Quest I'm never just sitting around trying to level
for--if I'm not XL14 after clearing the Valley, I'll go ahead with
parts of Gehennom rather than just sitting around levelling.

> 3) Do you make the effort of picking up every single item, even if you
> don't need it, in order to sell it in a shop - unless the load would
> burden you, or course? Even more, do you run back for items you left
> because you couldn't carry any more items (for the same purpose of
> selling them)?

No, but if it's early, I may run back to find stuff to sell if I find
a shop that's selling something useful.



